# Memcheck findings in dependencies that rind cannot fix in its own code.

# libcrux decides whether a tag verified, then branches on that decision. The
# outcome is public, but libcrux does not declassify it for memcheck.
{
   libcrux-aes-gcm-decrypt-outcome
   Memcheck:Cond
   src:aes_gcm.rs:99
   fun:*libcrux_aes*
}

# On armv7 without NEON, memcheck reports a condition in aws-lc's integer
# SHA-512. Every condition in it tests a round constant or the input pointer
# (sha512-armv4.s), never state or data, so the report comes from memcheck's
# flag tracking: each condition follows additions of secret words, whose carry
# memcheck can count against flags the condition never reads.
{
   aws-lc-sha512-armv4-nohw-flags
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:rind_*_sha512_block_data_order_nohw
}
